      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline. Taken on its own the patch is safe: the attach/detach refcounts balance and the locking matches pcc_file_open(). The gap shows up once the next patch in the chain lands. Separately, nothing tests the new detach_fid behaviour. If the patch is refreshed, consider a sanity-pcc case: attach -w, detach -k, then detach_fid while the inode is still cached, and check that the copy and the HSM archive are gone.",
