          "date": "2026-10-30 23:09:21.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-18298 pcc: pick up a lapsed copy in the detach ioctl",
        "message": "LU-18298 pcc: pick up a lapsed copy in the detach ioctl\n\npcc_ioctl_detach() returns success without removing the HSM archive\nwhen the client has no PCC inode attached, even though the copy is\nstill valid on the backend. \"lfs pcc detach -k\" leaves exactly that.\n\nIt has always relied on the caller having opened the file first, so\nthat pcc_file_open() re-attached it. Do that same PIT_OPEN attach in\nthe ioctl instead, under the dataset gating open uses, so no layout\nis refreshed and no lock is taken. \"lfs pcc detach_fid\" also picks\nup such a copy now, as long as the inode is still cached.\n\nThe next patch stops lfs pcc detach opening the file at all, which\nis what makes sanity-pcc test_16 depend on this.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nFixes: 2dadefb4148f (\"LU-10092 pcc: change detach behavior and add keep option\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I617ccd6fb847a6b368b4b107fb0fc9fc8ffae00f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
